================================================================================
This prompt (0001) and the sibling prompt 0012 BOTH template their native output to
`apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/ConfirmDialog.*` because their web sources share the basename
`ConfirmDialog.tsx`:
    0001 web source = components/ai/ConfirmDialog.tsx   (export AiConfirmDialog — AI tool approval)
    0012 web source = components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx   (export ConfirmDialog   — destructive action)
0012 is already committed + DONE at that exact path (see
.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/p4-apple-modals-dialogs-0012-ConfirmDialog.log) with the types
`ConfirmDialog`, `ConfirmDialogModel`, `ConfirmDialogProjection`, … and the diagnostics slug
"ConfirmDialog". Both surfaces compile into the ONE `TeslaSync` Swift module, so they cannot share a
filename OR type names (duplicate-symbol errors), and they cannot share a telemetry slug.

Resolution: this AI variant ships under the web component's own export name — `AiConfirmDialog` — for
its files (`AiConfirmDialog.*`), its types (`AiConfirmDialog*`), and its slug ("AiConfirmDialog").
The 0012 destructive-action surface is left byte-for-byte untouched (no predecessor bypass). This is
the only resolution that delivers BOTH surfaces; overwriting `ConfirmDialog.*` would have destroyed a
shipped sibling. The deviation is from the prompt's templated filename/slug only — the surface itself
is delivered in full, no scope narrowing.

